{
  "schema_version": "nexloop-business-object-types/1",
  "manifest_version": 2,
  "decision": "NX-026 D1 (dispatcher ruling 2026-10-10): NexLoop core business object types (M18 Commitment first), published at deployment through trusted configuration (0050) from this versioned declaration; never written to schema tables directly and never through the human review candidate path. Kept apart from system-object-types: those are system metadata never granted to any service principal, while business types are written by service principals through governed Actions (Commitment.create / Commitment.edit) and per-object derived authority (property_access_rules). v2 (NX-027): CommercialRecord, written only by the commercial_recorder service through CommercialRecord.create / CommercialRecord.edit with exactly the state SQL derives from verified signed commercial events (0130).",
  "object_types": [
    {
      "type_name": "Commitment",
